1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,620
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,440
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson.

3
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,640
J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,480
South India and educated in England.

5
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,989
For the past 40 years, he

6
00:00:48,989 --> 00:00:50,879
has been speaking in the United States,

7
00:00:50,879 --> 00:00:54,500
Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

8
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,100
From the outset of his life's work,

9
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,130
he repudiated all connections

10
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:01,160
with organized religions and ideologies

11
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:04,140
and said that his only concern

12
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,120
was to set men absolutely unconditionally free.

13
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,680
He is the author of many books, among them

14
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:14,320
The Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of Change,

15
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:18,160
Freedom from the Known, and The Flight of the Eagle.

16
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:21,800
This is one of a series of

17
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,380
dialogues between Krishnamurti and Dr. Alan W. Anderson,

18
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,860
who is professor of religious studies at

19
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:27,080
San Diego University.

20
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,280
Dr. Anderson is a professor at San Diego State University,

21
00:01:28,839 --> 00:01:30,679
where he teaches Indian and

22
00:01:30,679 --> 00:01:32,520
Chinese scriptures and the oracular tradition.

23
00:01:33,559 --> 00:01:36,009
Dr. Anderson, a published poet,

24
00:01:36,009 --> 00:01:38,460
received his degree from Columbia University

25
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:40,600
and the Union Theological Seminary.

26
00:01:41,179 --> 00:01:43,919
He has been honored with a Distinguished Teaching Award

27
00:01:43,919 --> 00:01:46,399
from the California State Universities.

28
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,300
Mr. Krishnamurti, just at the point where

29
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:53,100
we left last time in our conversation,

30
00:01:53,919 --> 00:01:57,100
we had raised the question of the distinction between

31
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:01,640
the notion that I must be responsible for my action

32
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:05,580
and just being responsible.

33
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:06,580
That's it.

34
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:11,180
I was sitting here thinking to myself,

35
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:12,540
oh, why can't we go on?

36
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:16,340
So perhaps we could start at that point.

37
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:16,940
Would that be agreeable?

38
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:19,859
I think, sir, there is a very definite distinction

39
00:02:19,859 --> 00:02:24,859
between responsible for and being responsible.

40
00:02:24,859 --> 00:02:26,859
If I...

41
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:34,620
Being responsible for implies a direction.

42
00:02:34,626 --> 00:02:36,466
えー

43
00:02:36,482 --> 00:02:39,182
a directed will.

44
00:02:39,182 --> 00:02:44,122
But the feeling of responsibility

45
00:02:44,142 --> 00:02:49,182
implies responsibility for everything,

46
00:02:49,182 --> 00:02:54,242
not in a direction, in any one particular direction.

47
00:02:54,242 --> 00:03:00,982
Responsible for education, responsible for politics,

48
00:03:00,982 --> 00:03:03,432
responsible for the way I

49
00:03:03,432 --> 00:03:05,882
live, responsible for my behaviour,

50
00:03:05,882 --> 00:03:11,882
it's a total feeling of complete responsibility,

51
00:03:11,882 --> 00:03:19,402
which is the ground in which action takes place.

52
00:03:20,562 --> 00:03:22,312
I think then this takes us

53
00:03:22,312 --> 00:03:24,062
back to this business of crisis

54
00:03:24,062 --> 00:03:25,762
we were talking about.

55
00:03:25,782 --> 00:03:33,262
If the crisis is continuous, then it's misleading to say,

56
00:03:33,262 --> 00:03:35,861
I'm responsible for my action,

57
00:03:35,862 --> 00:03:40,222
because I've put the thing out there again,

58
00:03:40,222 --> 00:03:42,942
and it becomes an occasion for

59
00:03:42,942 --> 00:03:45,662
my confusing what is at hand

60
00:03:45,682 --> 00:03:46,882
that requires to be done,

61
00:03:46,902 --> 00:03:50,542
and the concept of this notion of my action,

62
00:03:50,542 --> 00:03:52,342
because I am my action.

63
00:03:52,342 --> 00:03:54,842
Yes, that's it. I am it.

64
00:03:54,842 --> 00:03:58,982
That means I am...

65
00:03:58,982 --> 00:04:04,502
The feeling of responsibility expresses itself

66
00:04:04,502 --> 00:04:05,682
politically,

67
00:04:05,682 --> 00:04:05,842
politically,

68
00:04:05,842 --> 00:04:08,622
religiously, educationally, in business,

69
00:04:08,642 --> 00:04:11,882
in the whole of life,

70
00:04:11,902 --> 00:04:17,982
responsible for the total behaviour,

71
00:04:18,002 --> 00:04:22,521
not in a particular direction.

72
00:04:22,521 --> 00:04:25,622
I think there is a great deal of difference.

73
00:04:25,622 --> 00:04:32,082
When one says, I am responsible for my action,

74
00:04:32,082 --> 00:04:35,662
that means you are responsible for your action

75
00:04:35,662 --> 00:04:38,692
according to the idea that

76
00:04:38,692 --> 00:04:41,722
you have preconceived about action.

77
00:04:41,722 --> 00:04:45,722
Exactly. Yes.

78
00:04:45,742 --> 00:04:53,422
People sometimes will say that the child is free

79
00:04:53,422 --> 00:04:55,422
because it's not responsible.

80
00:04:55,422 --> 00:04:57,902
Oh, child is...

81
00:04:57,902 --> 00:04:59,222
You can't take a child...

82
00:04:59,222 --> 00:05:00,902
No, of course not.

83
00:05:00,902 --> 00:05:05,482
But I think sometimes when we say this,

84
00:05:05,482 --> 00:05:09,162
we have this nostalgia for the past,

85
00:05:09,182 --> 00:05:14,862
as though our freedom would be freedom from constraint.

86
00:05:14,882 --> 00:05:18,582
Whereas if one is his action genuinely, absolutely...

87
00:05:18,602 --> 00:05:19,782
There is no restraint.

88
00:05:19,802 --> 00:05:21,542
There isn't any restraint at all.

89
00:05:21,542 --> 00:05:23,622
None at all. Right.

90
00:05:23,622 --> 00:05:28,622
Because, sir, look, if one is totally...

91
00:05:28,642 --> 00:05:32,082
has this total feeling of responsibility,

92
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:35,302
then what is your responsibility?

93
00:05:35,302 --> 00:05:38,422
You have to have a

94
00:05:38,422 --> 00:05:41,542
responsibility with regard to your children.

95
00:05:41,542 --> 00:05:44,802
That means education.

96
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:50,322
Are you educating them to bring about a mind

97
00:05:50,322 --> 00:05:53,562
that conforms to the pattern

98
00:05:53,562 --> 00:05:56,802
which the society has established?

99
00:05:56,802 --> 00:06:00,222
Which means you accept the

100
00:06:00,222 --> 00:06:03,642
immorality of the society that is.

101
00:06:03,642 --> 00:06:05,082
Uh-huh.

102
00:06:05,082 --> 00:06:06,962
Totally responsible you are.

103
00:06:06,962 --> 00:06:10,462
Responsible from the moment it's

104
00:06:10,462 --> 00:06:13,962
born till the moment it dies.

105
00:06:13,962 --> 00:06:17,322
The right kind of education,

106
00:06:17,322 --> 00:06:23,841
not the education of making the child conform,

107
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:26,082
and the worship of success,

108
00:06:26,082 --> 00:06:31,082
and the division of nationalities which brings about war.

109
00:06:31,082 --> 00:06:35,082
You follow? All that you are responsible for.

110
00:06:35,082 --> 00:06:38,582
Not just in a particular direction.

111
00:06:38,582 --> 00:06:41,462
Even if you are in a particular direction,

112
00:06:41,462 --> 00:06:43,582
I am responsible for my act,

113
00:06:43,582 --> 00:06:46,922
what is your action based on?

114
00:06:46,922 --> 00:06:49,582
How can you be responsible

115
00:06:49,582 --> 00:06:55,082
when your action is the result of a formula

116
00:06:55,082 --> 00:07:00,082
that has been handed down to you?

117
00:07:00,082 --> 00:07:02,462
Yes, I quite follow what you mean.

118
00:07:02,462 --> 00:07:04,201
Like communists,

119
00:07:04,201 --> 00:07:05,082
they are...

120
00:07:05,082 --> 00:07:12,082
They say the state is responsible.

121
00:07:12,082 --> 00:07:14,082
The state worships the state.

122
00:07:14,082 --> 00:07:17,582
The state is the god.

123
00:07:17,582 --> 00:07:21,582
And you are responsible to the state.

124
00:07:21,582 --> 00:07:28,582
Which means they have conceived what the state should be,

125
00:07:28,582 --> 00:07:31,582
formulated ideationally,

126
00:07:31,582 --> 00:07:35,082
and according to that you act.

127
00:07:35,082 --> 00:07:38,082
That is not responsible action.

128
00:07:38,082 --> 00:07:42,082
That is irresponsible action.

129
00:07:42,082 --> 00:07:46,082
Whereas action means the doing now,

130
00:07:46,082 --> 00:07:50,082
the active present of the verb to do,

131
00:07:50,082 --> 00:07:54,082
which is to do now, the acting now.

132
00:07:54,082 --> 00:07:59,082
The acting now must be free from the past.

133
00:07:59,082 --> 00:08:05,082
Otherwise you are just repeating, repetition.

134
00:08:05,082 --> 00:08:08,082
Traditionally, adding on. That is not...

135
00:08:08,082 --> 00:08:14,082
I am reminded of something in the I Ching

136
00:08:14,082 --> 00:08:19,082
that I think is a reflection of this principle

137
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:21,082
that you pointed to.

138
00:08:21,082 --> 00:08:26,082
I don't mean principle in the abstract.

139
00:08:26,082 --> 00:08:28,082
If I am quoting it correctly

140
00:08:28,082 --> 00:08:30,082
from one of the standard translations,

141
00:08:30,082 --> 00:08:32,082
it goes like this,

142
00:08:32,082 --> 00:08:35,082
the superior man, by which it means the superior,

143
00:08:35,082 --> 00:08:42,082
the free man, not hierarchically structured,

144
00:08:42,082 --> 00:08:47,082
does not let his thoughts go beyond his situation.

145
00:08:47,082 --> 00:08:52,582
Which would mean that he simply

146
00:08:52,582 --> 00:08:58,082
would be present as he is,

147
00:08:58,082 --> 00:09:01,082
not being responsible to something out there

148
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:04,082
that is going to tell him how to be responsible,

149
00:09:04,082 --> 00:09:07,082
what he should do.

150
00:09:07,082 --> 00:09:10,082
But upon the instant that he is,

151
00:09:10,082 --> 00:09:12,082
he is always...

152
00:09:12,082 --> 00:09:13,082
Responsible.

153
00:09:13,082 --> 00:09:14,082
Responsible.

154
00:09:14,082 --> 00:09:16,082
He simply does not let

155
00:09:16,082 --> 00:09:18,082
his thoughts go beyond his situation.

156
00:09:18,082 --> 00:09:20,082
That goes back to that word negation.

157
00:09:20,082 --> 00:09:21,582
Because if he won't let

158
00:09:21,582 --> 00:09:23,082
his thoughts go beyond his situation,

159
00:09:23,082 --> 00:09:24,582
he has negated the possibility

160
00:09:24,582 --> 00:09:26,082
for their doing so, hasn't he?

161
00:09:26,082 --> 00:09:27,082
Yes.

162
00:09:27,082 --> 00:09:31,082
Oh yes, yes, yes, I see that.

163
00:09:31,082 --> 00:09:33,082
The reason that I am referring to these

164
00:09:33,082 --> 00:09:42,082
other quotations is because

165
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:47,082
if what you are saying is true,

166
00:09:47,082 --> 00:09:51,082
and if what they say is true,

167
00:09:51,082 --> 00:09:54,082
quite without respect to how they are understood

168
00:09:54,082 --> 00:09:55,082
or not understood,

169
00:09:55,082 --> 00:09:59,082
then there must be something in common here.

170
00:09:59,082 --> 00:10:03,082
And I realize that your emphasis is on

171
00:10:03,082 --> 00:10:08,082
practical, eminently practical, upon the act.

172
00:10:08,082 --> 00:10:09,582
But it does seem to

173
00:10:09,582 --> 00:10:11,082
me to be of great value

174
00:10:11,082 --> 00:10:23,082
if one could converse, commune with the great literatures

175
00:10:23,082 --> 00:10:25,082
which have so many statements in them

176
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:29,082
that complain about the fact that they are not understood.

177
00:10:29,082 --> 00:10:31,082
I see that as a great gain.

178
00:10:31,082 --> 00:10:32,082
So...

179
00:10:33,082 --> 00:10:42,082
I have not read any books,

180
00:10:42,082 --> 00:10:45,082
any literature in the sense...

181
00:10:45,082 --> 00:10:46,082
Yes, sir, I understand.

182
00:10:46,082 --> 00:10:50,082
...in that sense.

183
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:54,082
Suppose there is no book in the world.

184
00:10:54,082 --> 00:10:56,082
Problem is the same.

185
00:10:56,082 --> 00:10:58,082
Problem is the same.

186
00:10:58,082 --> 00:11:00,082
Of course, of course.

187
00:11:00,082 --> 00:11:02,082
There is no leader, no teacher,

188
00:11:02,082 --> 00:11:03,082
nobody to tell you,

189
00:11:03,082 --> 00:11:06,082
do this, do that, don't do this, don't do that.

190
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:08,082
You are there.

191
00:11:08,082 --> 00:11:14,082
You feel totally, completely responsible.

192
00:11:14,082 --> 00:11:16,082
Right. Yes.

193
00:11:16,082 --> 00:11:21,082
Then you have to have an astonishingly active,

194
00:11:21,082 --> 00:11:25,082
clear brain.

195
00:11:25,082 --> 00:11:30,082
Not befuddled, not puzzled, not bewildered.

196
00:11:30,082 --> 00:11:32,082
You must have a mind that thinks clearly,

197
00:11:32,082 --> 00:11:33,082
clearly.

198
00:11:33,082 --> 00:11:35,082
And you cannot think clearly

199
00:11:35,082 --> 00:11:39,082
if you are rooted in the past.

200
00:11:39,082 --> 00:11:43,082
You are merely continuing, modified perhaps,

201
00:11:43,082 --> 00:11:44,082
through the present to the future.

202
00:11:44,082 --> 00:11:47,082
That's all.

203
00:11:47,082 --> 00:11:52,082
So, from that arises the question,

204
00:11:52,082 --> 00:12:01,082
what is the responsibility in human relationship?

205
00:12:02,082 --> 00:12:04,082
Yes, now we are back to relationship.

206
00:12:04,082 --> 00:12:05,082
Relationship.

207
00:12:05,082 --> 00:12:14,082
Because that is the basic foundation of life.

208
00:12:14,082 --> 00:12:18,082
Relationship, that is to be related,

209
00:12:18,082 --> 00:12:21,082
to be in contact with.

210
00:12:21,082 --> 00:12:24,082
We are presently related.

211
00:12:24,082 --> 00:12:26,082
This is what is.

212
00:12:26,082 --> 00:12:27,082
Yes.

213
00:12:27,082 --> 00:12:31,082
Now, what is human relationship?

214
00:12:32,082 --> 00:12:38,082
If I feel totally responsible,

215
00:12:38,082 --> 00:12:46,082
how does that responsibility express in relationship?

216
00:12:46,082 --> 00:12:49,082
To my children, if I have children,

217
00:12:49,082 --> 00:12:52,082
to my family, to my neighbour,

218
00:12:52,082 --> 00:12:55,082
whether the neighbour is next door

219
00:12:55,082 --> 00:12:57,082
or ten thousand miles away,

220
00:12:57,082 --> 00:13:00,082
is still my neighbour.

221
00:13:00,082 --> 00:13:02,082
So what is my responsibility?

222
00:13:02,082 --> 00:13:06,082
What is the responsibility of a man

223
00:13:06,082 --> 00:13:10,082
who feels totally,

224
00:13:10,082 --> 00:13:15,082
completely involved in this feeling

225
00:13:15,082 --> 00:13:19,082
of being a light to himself

226
00:13:19,082 --> 00:13:23,082
and totally responsible?

227
00:13:23,082 --> 00:13:26,082
I think this is a question, sir,

228
00:13:26,082 --> 00:13:30,082
that has to be investigated,

229
00:13:30,082 --> 00:13:33,082
which is not a question of the mind.

230
00:13:33,082 --> 00:13:35,082
Yes, you know what I am thinking?

231
00:13:35,082 --> 00:13:41,082
I am thinking that only a person responsible,

232
00:13:41,082 --> 00:13:43,082
as you have said it,

233
00:13:43,082 --> 00:13:45,082
can make what we call in our tongue

234
00:13:45,082 --> 00:13:47,082
a clean decision.

235
00:13:47,082 --> 00:13:49,082
Of course, of course.

236
00:13:49,082 --> 00:13:57,082
So many decisions are frayed, are...

237
00:13:57,082 --> 00:14:00,082
Sir, I would like to ask this.

238
00:14:00,082 --> 00:14:05,082
Is there a decision at all?

239
00:14:06,082 --> 00:14:09,082
Decision implies choice.

240
00:14:09,082 --> 00:14:12,082
Yes.

241
00:14:12,082 --> 00:14:15,082
Choice implies a mind that is confused

242
00:14:15,082 --> 00:14:17,082
between this and that.

243
00:14:17,082 --> 00:14:21,082
It means, I think, radically to make a cut,

244
00:14:21,082 --> 00:14:23,082
to cut off.

245
00:14:23,082 --> 00:14:29,082
Yes, but a mind that sees clearly has no choice.

246
00:14:29,082 --> 00:14:30,082
It doesn't decide.

247
00:14:30,082 --> 00:14:33,082
It acts.

248
00:14:33,082 --> 00:14:34,082
Yes.

249
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:37,082
Doesn't this take us back to this word negation again?

250
00:14:37,082 --> 00:14:39,082
Yes, of course.

251
00:14:39,082 --> 00:14:41,082
Might it not be that a clean decision

252
00:14:41,082 --> 00:14:43,082
could be interpreted in terms

253
00:14:43,082 --> 00:14:46,082
of what takes place at this point of negation?

254
00:14:46,082 --> 00:14:47,082
Yes.

255
00:14:47,082 --> 00:14:50,082
From which flows a different action...

256
00:14:50,082 --> 00:14:54,082
But I don't like to use that word decision.

257
00:14:54,082 --> 00:14:58,082
Because the deciding between this and that...

258
00:14:58,082 --> 00:15:00,082
You know, sir,

259
00:15:00,082 --> 00:15:02,082
you don't want to use it because of

260
00:15:02,082 --> 00:15:04,082
the implications in it of conflict.

261
00:15:04,082 --> 00:15:05,082
Conflict.

262
00:15:05,082 --> 00:15:06,082
Conflict.

263
00:15:06,082 --> 00:15:07,082
I see, I see.

264
00:15:07,082 --> 00:15:10,082
Choice.

265
00:15:10,082 --> 00:15:13,082
We think we are free because we choose.

266
00:15:13,082 --> 00:15:16,082
We can choose. Right?

267
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:23,082
Is a mind free that is capable of choice?

268
00:15:23,082 --> 00:15:29,082
Or is a mind that is not free that chooses?

269
00:15:29,082 --> 00:15:34,082
Choice implies between this and that.

270
00:15:34,082 --> 00:15:36,082
Obviously.

271
00:15:36,082 --> 00:15:42,082
Now, which means the mind doesn't see clearly

272
00:15:42,082 --> 00:15:44,082
and therefore there is choice.

273
00:15:44,082 --> 00:15:47,082
Choice exists when there is confusion.

274
00:15:47,082 --> 00:15:50,082
Yes, yes, yes.

275
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:52,082
Mind that sees clearly, there is no choice.

276
00:15:52,082 --> 00:15:56,082
It is doing.

277
00:15:56,082 --> 00:15:58,082
I mean, I think that is...

278
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:00,582
I think this is where

279
00:16:00,582 --> 00:16:03,082
we have got into rather trouble

280
00:16:03,082 --> 00:16:06,082
when we say we are free to choose.

281
00:16:06,082 --> 00:16:09,082
Choice implies freedom.

282
00:16:09,082 --> 00:16:11,082
I say on the contrary.

283
00:16:11,082 --> 00:16:14,082
Choice implies a mind that is confused

284
00:16:14,082 --> 00:16:18,082
and therefore not free.

285
00:16:18,082 --> 00:16:25,082
What occurs to me now is the difference between

286
00:16:25,082 --> 00:16:28,082
regarding freedom,

287
00:16:28,082 --> 00:16:30,082
as a property or quality of action,

288
00:16:30,082 --> 00:16:32,082
rather than a state.

289
00:16:32,082 --> 00:16:33,082
Oh!

290
00:16:33,082 --> 00:16:34,082
Yes.

291
00:16:34,082 --> 00:16:38,082
But we have the notion that freedom is a state,

292
00:16:38,082 --> 00:16:40,082
a condition,

293
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:43,082
which is quite different from the emphasis

294
00:16:43,082 --> 00:16:45,082
that you are leading me into.

295
00:16:45,082 --> 00:16:46,082
Yes, that's right.

296
00:16:46,082 --> 00:16:48,082
Yes, yes, yes.

297
00:16:48,082 --> 00:16:50,082
So let's come back to this, I think, sir,

298
00:16:50,082 --> 00:16:54,082
which is, what is the responsibility

299
00:16:54,082 --> 00:16:57,082
of a human being

300
00:16:57,082 --> 00:16:58,082
who feels free?

301
00:16:58,082 --> 00:17:05,082
Who has this sense of responsibility in relationship?

302
00:17:05,082 --> 00:17:08,082
Because relationship is life.

303
00:17:08,082 --> 00:17:13,082
Relationship is the foundation of existence.

304
00:17:13,082 --> 00:17:17,082
Relationship is absolutely necessary,

305
00:17:17,082 --> 00:17:19,082
otherwise you can't exist.

306
00:17:19,082 --> 00:17:22,082
Relationship means cooperation.

307
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:27,082
Everything is involved in that one word.

308
00:17:27,082 --> 00:17:30,082
Relationship means love and generosity

309
00:17:30,082 --> 00:17:32,082
and all that's implied.

310
00:17:32,082 --> 00:17:39,082
Now, what is a human responsibility

311
00:17:39,082 --> 00:17:42,082
in relationship?

312
00:17:42,082 --> 00:17:48,082
If we were genuinely and completely sharing,

313
00:17:48,082 --> 00:17:53,082
then responsibility would be present, fully.

314
00:17:53,082 --> 00:17:56,082
Yes, but how does it express itself

315
00:17:56,082 --> 00:18:01,082
in relationship?

316
00:18:01,082 --> 00:18:03,082
Not only between you and me now,

317
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,082
but between man and woman,

318
00:18:05,082 --> 00:18:09,082
between my neighbour,

319
00:18:09,082 --> 00:18:10,082
between...

320
00:18:10,082 --> 00:18:13,082
Relationship, sir, to everything, to nature.

321
00:18:13,082 --> 00:18:18,082
What's my relationship to nature?

322
00:18:18,082 --> 00:18:23,082
Would I go and kill the baby seals?

323
00:18:23,082 --> 00:18:25,082
No, no.

324
00:18:25,082 --> 00:18:31,082
Would I go and destroy human beings,

325
00:18:31,082 --> 00:18:36,082
calling them enemies?

326
00:18:36,082 --> 00:18:39,082
Would I destroy nature,

327
00:18:39,082 --> 00:18:42,082
everything which man is doing now?

328
00:18:42,082 --> 00:18:46,082
He is destroying the earth, the air, the sea, everything.

329
00:18:46,082 --> 00:18:51,082
Because he feels totally irresponsible.

330
00:18:51,082 --> 00:18:54,082
He sees what is out there

331
00:18:54,082 --> 00:18:56,082
as something to operate on.

332
00:18:56,082 --> 00:19:00,082
Yes, which is, he kills the baby seal,

333
00:19:00,082 --> 00:19:02,082
which I saw the other day in a film,

334
00:19:02,082 --> 00:19:04,082
which is an appalling thing.

335
00:19:04,082 --> 00:19:07,082
And a Christian, they call themselves Christians,

336
00:19:07,082 --> 00:19:09,082
going killing a little thing

337
00:19:09,082 --> 00:19:11,082
for somebody's...

338
00:19:11,082 --> 00:19:14,082
for some lady to put on the fur.

339
00:19:14,082 --> 00:19:18,082
And you follow,

340
00:19:18,082 --> 00:19:21,082
it's totally immoral, the whole thing is.

341
00:19:21,082 --> 00:19:24,082
So, to come back, I say,

342
00:19:24,082 --> 00:19:28,082
what is, how does this responsibility

343
00:19:28,082 --> 00:19:33,082
show itself in my life?

344
00:19:33,082 --> 00:19:35,082
I'm married.

345
00:19:35,082 --> 00:19:38,082
I'm not, but suppose I'm married.

346
00:19:38,082 --> 00:19:41,081
What is my responsibility?

347
00:19:41,081 --> 00:19:46,081
Am I related to my wife?

348
00:19:46,081 --> 00:19:48,081
The record doesn't seem very good.

349
00:19:48,081 --> 00:19:50,081
No, not only record, actuality.

350
00:19:50,081 --> 00:19:52,081
Am I related to my wife?

351
00:19:52,081 --> 00:19:54,081
Or am I related to my wife

352
00:19:54,081 --> 00:19:59,081
according to the image I have built about her?

353
00:19:59,081 --> 00:20:01,081
And I'm responsible for that image.

354
00:20:01,081 --> 00:20:02,081
You follow, sir?

355
00:20:02,081 --> 00:20:05,082
Yes, because my input has been continuous

356
00:20:05,082 --> 00:20:06,082
with respect to that image.

357
00:20:06,082 --> 00:20:13,082
Yes. So, I have no relationship with my wife

358
00:20:13,082 --> 00:20:16,082
if I have an image about her.

359
00:20:16,082 --> 00:20:18,082
Or if I have an image about myself

360
00:20:18,082 --> 00:20:20,082
when I want to be successful,

361
00:20:20,082 --> 00:20:23,082
all the rest of that business.

362
00:20:23,082 --> 00:20:27,082
Since we were talking about now,

363
00:20:27,082 --> 00:20:29,082
being now,

364
00:20:29,082 --> 00:20:34,082
there's a point of contact, I take it,

365
00:20:34,082 --> 00:20:36,082
between what you're saying

366
00:20:36,082 --> 00:20:38,082
and the phrase that you used

367
00:20:38,082 --> 00:20:40,082
in one of our earlier conversations,

368
00:20:40,082 --> 00:20:42,082
the betrayal of the present.

369
00:20:42,082 --> 00:20:43,082
Absolutely.

370
00:20:43,082 --> 00:20:46,082
Yes. If one...

371
00:20:46,082 --> 00:20:49,082
You see, that is the whole point, sir.

372
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:53,082
If I am related to you,

373
00:20:53,082 --> 00:20:55,082
I have no image about you

374
00:20:55,082 --> 00:20:58,082
or you have an image about me.

375
00:20:58,082 --> 00:21:02,082
Then we have relationship.

376
00:21:02,082 --> 00:21:04,082
We have no relationship

377
00:21:04,082 --> 00:21:06,082
if I have an image about myself

378
00:21:06,082 --> 00:21:09,082
or about you.

379
00:21:09,082 --> 00:21:13,082
Our images have a relationship.

380
00:21:13,082 --> 00:21:17,082
But in actuality, we have no relationship.

381
00:21:17,082 --> 00:21:19,082
I may sleep with my wife or with some,

382
00:21:19,082 --> 00:21:22,082
but it is not a relationship.

383
00:21:22,082 --> 00:21:26,082
It is a physical contact,

384
00:21:26,082 --> 00:21:31,082
sensory excitement, nothing else.

385
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:37,082
So my responsibility is not to have an image.

386
00:21:37,082 --> 00:21:43,082
This brings to mind,

387
00:21:43,082 --> 00:21:51,082
I think, one of the loveliest statements

388
00:21:51,082 --> 00:21:52,082
in the English language,

389
00:21:52,082 --> 00:21:55,082
which I should like to understand

390
00:21:55,082 --> 00:21:59,082
in terms of what we have been sharing.

391
00:21:59,082 --> 00:22:04,082
These lines from Keats' poem, Endymion.

392
00:22:04,082 --> 00:22:07,082
There's something miraculous, marvelous

393
00:22:07,082 --> 00:22:10,082
in this statement, it seems to me,

394
00:22:10,082 --> 00:22:12,082
that's immediately related

395
00:22:12,082 --> 00:22:15,082
to what you've been saying.

396
00:22:15,082 --> 00:22:20,082
A thing of beauty is a joy forever.

397
00:22:20,082 --> 00:22:22,082
And then he says,

398
00:22:22,082 --> 00:22:24,082
as though that's not enough,

399
00:22:24,082 --> 00:22:28,082
he says, its loveliness increases.

400
00:22:28,082 --> 00:22:30,082
Quite, quite.

401
00:22:30,082 --> 00:22:32,082
And then as though that's not enough,

402
00:22:32,082 --> 00:22:37,082
he says, it will never pass into nothingness.

403
00:22:37,082 --> 00:22:39,082
Quite.

404
00:22:39,082 --> 00:22:46,082
Now, when the present is not betrayed,

405
00:22:46,082 --> 00:22:52,082
it's full with a fullness.

406
00:22:52,082 --> 00:22:54,082
That keeps on abounding.

407
00:22:54,082 --> 00:22:56,082
It's quite understandable.

408
00:22:56,082 --> 00:22:57,082
Would I be correct in that?

409
00:22:57,082 --> 00:22:58,082
Yes, I think so.

410
00:22:58,082 --> 00:23:02,082
I think that's truly what he must be saying.

411
00:23:02,082 --> 00:23:04,582
And one of the things,

412
00:23:04,582 --> 00:23:07,082
too, that passed my mind was,

413
00:23:07,082 --> 00:23:10,082
he calls it a thing of beauty.

414
00:23:10,082 --> 00:23:12,082
He doesn't call it a beautiful thing.

415
00:23:12,082 --> 00:23:13,082
No.

416
00:23:13,082 --> 00:23:15,082
No, it's a thing of beauty,

417
00:23:15,082 --> 00:23:18,082
as though it's a child of beauty.

418
00:23:18,082 --> 00:23:20,082
Marvellous continuity between this.

419
00:23:20,082 --> 00:23:21,082
Not it's beautiful

420
00:23:21,082 --> 00:23:22,082
because I think it's beautiful,

421
00:23:22,082 --> 00:23:24,082
and therefore it's outside.

422
00:23:24,082 --> 00:23:27,082
This...

423
00:23:27,082 --> 00:23:29,082
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

424
00:23:29,082 --> 00:23:30,082
I must stick to this,

425
00:23:30,082 --> 00:23:33,082
because this is really quite important.

426
00:23:33,082 --> 00:23:40,082
Because you go where you will,

427
00:23:40,082 --> 00:23:46,082
there is no relationship between human beings.

428
00:23:46,082 --> 00:23:49,082
And that is the tragedy,

429
00:23:49,082 --> 00:23:51,082
and from that arises the truth.

430
00:23:51,082 --> 00:23:55,082
Because all our conflict, violence,

431
00:23:55,082 --> 00:23:57,082
the whole business.

432
00:23:57,082 --> 00:23:59,082
So, if...

433
00:23:59,082 --> 00:24:00,082
No, not if.

434
00:24:00,082 --> 00:24:03,082
When there is this responsibility,

435
00:24:03,082 --> 00:24:05,082
the feeling of this responsibility,

436
00:24:05,082 --> 00:24:09,082
it translates itself in relationship,

437
00:24:09,082 --> 00:24:13,082
it doesn't matter with whom it is,

438
00:24:13,082 --> 00:24:17,082
a freedom from the known,

439
00:24:17,082 --> 00:24:20,082
which is the image.

440
00:24:21,082 --> 00:24:24,082
And therefore, in that freedom,

441
00:24:24,082 --> 00:24:27,082
goodness flowers.

442
00:24:27,082 --> 00:24:29,082
Goodness flowers.

443
00:24:29,082 --> 00:24:31,082
And that is the beauty.

444
00:24:31,082 --> 00:24:33,082
And that is beauty.

445
00:24:33,082 --> 00:24:36,082
Beauty is not an abstract thing,

446
00:24:36,082 --> 00:24:39,082
but it goes with goodness.

447
00:24:39,082 --> 00:24:41,082
Goodness in behaviour,

448
00:24:41,082 --> 00:24:42,082
goodness in conduct,

449
00:24:42,082 --> 00:24:45,082
goodness in action.

450
00:24:45,082 --> 00:24:47,082
Sometimes while we've been talking,

451
00:24:47,082 --> 00:24:49,082
I've started a sentence with, if...

452
00:24:49,082 --> 00:24:50,082
Oh, yes.

453
00:24:50,082 --> 00:24:53,082
And I've looked into your eyes,

454
00:24:53,082 --> 00:24:55,082
and immediately I got it out,

455
00:24:55,082 --> 00:24:57,082
I knew I'd said the wrong thing.

456
00:24:57,082 --> 00:24:58,082
It's just like a minute ago,

457
00:24:58,082 --> 00:25:00,082
you said if, and you said no, when.

458
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:01,082
Yes.

459
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,082
We are always if-ing it up.

460
00:25:03,082 --> 00:25:05,082
I know, if-ing it up.

461
00:25:05,082 --> 00:25:07,082
It is, it's awful.

462
00:25:07,082 --> 00:25:08,082
I know, sir.

463
00:25:08,082 --> 00:25:10,082
We are always dealing with abstractions

464
00:25:10,082 --> 00:25:13,082
rather than with reality.

465
00:25:13,082 --> 00:25:15,082
Immediately we if.

466
00:25:15,082 --> 00:25:17,082
A construction is out there,

467
00:25:17,082 --> 00:25:19,082
which we endlessly talk about.

468
00:25:19,082 --> 00:25:20,082
That's right.

469
00:25:20,082 --> 00:25:23,082
And we get cleverer and cleverer about it.

470
00:25:23,082 --> 00:25:26,082
And it has nothing to do with anything.

471
00:25:26,082 --> 00:25:29,082
Yes, yes, yes.

472
00:25:29,082 --> 00:25:34,082
So, how does this responsibility

473
00:25:34,082 --> 00:25:39,082
translate itself in human behaviour?

474
00:25:39,082 --> 00:25:41,082
You follow, sir?

475
00:25:41,082 --> 00:25:44,082
Uh-huh.

476
00:25:44,082 --> 00:25:47,082
There would be an end to violence.

477
00:25:47,082 --> 00:25:49,082
Absolutely.

478
00:25:49,082 --> 00:25:52,082
Wouldn't taper off.

479
00:25:54,082 --> 00:25:57,082
You see what we have done, sir?

480
00:25:57,082 --> 00:25:58,082
We have taken...

481
00:25:58,082 --> 00:26:00,082
We are violent human beings,

482
00:26:00,082 --> 00:26:03,082
sexually, morally, in every way

483
00:26:03,082 --> 00:26:05,082
we are violent human beings.

484
00:26:05,082 --> 00:26:08,082
And not being able to resolve it,

485
00:26:08,082 --> 00:26:11,082
we have created an ideal

486
00:26:11,082 --> 00:26:15,082
of not being violent,

487
00:26:15,082 --> 00:26:18,082
which is the fact

488
00:26:18,082 --> 00:26:21,082
and abstraction of the fact,

489
00:26:21,082 --> 00:26:24,082
which is non-fact,

490
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:28,082
and try to live the non-fact.

491
00:26:28,082 --> 00:26:29,082
Yes.

492
00:26:29,082 --> 00:26:31,082
Immediately that produces conflict

493
00:26:31,082 --> 00:26:32,082
because it can't be done.

494
00:26:32,082 --> 00:26:34,082
It produces conflict, misery, confusion,

495
00:26:34,082 --> 00:26:35,082
all the rest of it.

496
00:26:35,082 --> 00:26:40,082
Now, why does the mind do it?

497
00:26:40,082 --> 00:26:43,082
The mind does it because

498
00:26:43,082 --> 00:26:45,082
it doesn't know what to

499
00:26:45,082 --> 00:26:47,082
do with this fact of violence.

500
00:26:47,082 --> 00:26:50,082
Therefore, in abstracting,

501
00:26:50,082 --> 00:26:54,082
the idea of not being violent

502
00:26:54,082 --> 00:26:57,082
postpones action.

503
00:26:57,082 --> 00:26:58,082
Uh-huh.

504
00:26:58,082 --> 00:27:01,082
I am trying not to be violent.

505
00:27:01,082 --> 00:27:05,082
And in the meantime, I am jolly well violent.

506
00:27:05,082 --> 00:27:07,082
Yes.

507
00:27:07,082 --> 00:27:12,082
And it is an escape from the fact.

508
00:27:12,082 --> 00:27:16,082
All abstractions are escape from the fact.

509
00:27:17,082 --> 00:27:20,082
So, the mind does it because

510
00:27:20,082 --> 00:27:24,082
it is incapable of dealing with the fact,

511
00:27:24,082 --> 00:27:28,082
or it doesn't want to deal with the fact,

512
00:27:28,082 --> 00:27:31,082
or it is lazy and says,

513
00:27:31,082 --> 00:27:35,082
well, I will try and do it some other day.

514
00:27:35,082 --> 00:27:36,082
All those are involved

515
00:27:36,082 --> 00:27:41,082
when it withdraws from the fact.

516
00:27:41,082 --> 00:27:44,082
Now, in the same way,

517
00:27:44,082 --> 00:27:46,082
the fact is,

518
00:27:46,082 --> 00:27:51,082
our relationship is non-existent.

519
00:27:51,082 --> 00:27:52,082
I may say to my wife,

520
00:27:52,082 --> 00:27:54,082
I love you, I am, etc., etc.,

521
00:27:54,082 --> 00:27:57,082
but it is non-existent.

522
00:27:57,082 --> 00:27:59,082
Because I have an image about her

523
00:27:59,082 --> 00:28:02,082
and she has an image about me.

524
00:28:02,082 --> 00:28:07,082
So, on abstractions we have lived.

525
00:28:07,082 --> 00:28:12,082
It just occurred to me that the word fact itself,

526
00:28:12,082 --> 00:28:15,082
which there have been no end of disquisitions about...

527
00:28:15,082 --> 00:28:16,082
Ah, of course.

528
00:28:16,082 --> 00:28:18,082
Fact, what is, let's call it what is.

529
00:28:18,082 --> 00:28:22,082
But actually it means something done.

530
00:28:22,082 --> 00:28:23,082
Done, yes.

531
00:28:23,082 --> 00:28:25,082
Not the record of something,

532
00:28:25,082 --> 00:28:29,082
but actually something done, performed,

533
00:28:29,082 --> 00:28:31,082
act, act.

534
00:28:31,082 --> 00:28:33,082
And it is that sense of fact

535
00:28:33,082 --> 00:28:37,082
that with our use of the word fact,

536
00:28:37,082 --> 00:28:38,082
give me facts and figures,

537
00:28:38,082 --> 00:28:40,082
we say in English, give me facts...

538
00:28:40,082 --> 00:28:42,082
We don't mean that when we say it.

539
00:28:42,082 --> 00:28:43,082
No.

540
00:28:43,082 --> 00:28:45,082
No, no.

541
00:28:45,082 --> 00:28:48,082
One probably wouldn't need facts and figures

542
00:28:48,082 --> 00:28:51,082
in that abstract sense.

543
00:28:51,082 --> 00:28:55,082
You see, sir, this reveals a tremendous lot...

544
00:28:55,082 --> 00:28:57,082
I follow.

545
00:28:57,082 --> 00:28:59,082
...when you feel responsible.

546
00:28:59,082 --> 00:29:04,082
You feel responsible for education of your children.

547
00:29:04,082 --> 00:29:09,082
Not only your children, children.

548
00:29:09,082 --> 00:29:13,082
Are you educating them

549
00:29:13,082 --> 00:29:15,082
to conform to a society

550
00:29:15,082 --> 00:29:20,082
or are you educating them to merely acquire a job?

551
00:29:20,082 --> 00:29:24,582
Are you educating them to

552
00:29:24,582 --> 00:29:29,082
the continuity of what has been?

553
00:29:29,082 --> 00:29:37,082
Are you educating them to live in abstractions,

554
00:29:37,082 --> 00:29:40,082
as we are doing now?

555
00:29:40,082 --> 00:29:44,082
So what is your responsibility

556
00:29:44,082 --> 00:29:46,082
as a father, mother,

557
00:29:46,082 --> 00:29:48,082
it doesn't matter who you are,

558
00:29:48,082 --> 00:29:51,082
responsible in education,

559
00:29:51,082 --> 00:29:56,082
for the education of a human being?

560
00:29:59,082 --> 00:30:01,082
That's one problem.

561
00:30:01,082 --> 00:30:05,082
What is your responsibility

562
00:30:05,082 --> 00:30:13,082
if you feel responsible for human growth,

563
00:30:13,082 --> 00:30:17,082
human culture, human goodness?

564
00:30:17,082 --> 00:30:19,082
You?

565
00:30:19,082 --> 00:30:25,082
What is your responsibility to the earth?

566
00:30:25,082 --> 00:30:27,082
To nature? You follow?

567
00:30:27,082 --> 00:30:36,082
It is a tremendous thing to feel responsible.

568
00:30:36,082 --> 00:30:41,082
This just came to mind,

569
00:30:41,082 --> 00:30:45,082
which I must ask you about.

570
00:30:45,082 --> 00:30:48,082
The word negation in the book

571
00:30:48,082 --> 00:30:50,082
that we looked at earlier,

572
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:56,082
which is continuous with what we are saying,

573
00:30:56,082 --> 00:31:03,082
I think is itself rather endangered

574
00:31:03,082 --> 00:31:08,082
by the usual notion that we have of negation,

575
00:31:08,082 --> 00:31:10,082
which is simply a prohibition,

576
00:31:10,082 --> 00:31:12,082
which is not meant.

577
00:31:12,082 --> 00:31:13,082
No.

578
00:31:13,082 --> 00:31:14,082
Which is not meant.

579
00:31:14,082 --> 00:31:16,082
Of course.

580
00:31:16,082 --> 00:31:20,082
When we reviewed that incident in the Gita

581
00:31:20,082 --> 00:31:22,082
between the general and his charioteer,

582
00:31:22,082 --> 00:31:27,082
the Lord Krishna,

583
00:31:27,082 --> 00:31:33,082
the Lord's response was a negation

584
00:31:33,082 --> 00:31:36,082
without it being a prohibition.

585
00:31:36,082 --> 00:31:37,082
Quite, quite.

586
00:31:37,082 --> 00:31:38,082
Wasn't it?

587
00:31:38,082 --> 00:31:39,082
I don't know.

588
00:31:39,082 --> 00:31:40,082
No, no, I mean in terms

589
00:31:40,082 --> 00:31:41,082
of what we just got through seeing.

590
00:31:41,082 --> 00:31:42,082
Yes, of course.

591
00:31:42,082 --> 00:31:43,082
Yes.

592
00:31:46,082 --> 00:31:51,082
There is a difference then between

593
00:31:51,082 --> 00:31:57,082
rearing a child in terms of

594
00:31:57,082 --> 00:32:01,082
relating to the child radically in the present,

595
00:32:01,082 --> 00:32:04,082
in which negation, as is mentioned in the book here

596
00:32:04,082 --> 00:32:06,082
that we went through,

597
00:32:06,082 --> 00:32:08,082
is continuously

598
00:32:08,082 --> 00:32:14,082
and immediately and actively present,

599
00:32:14,082 --> 00:32:18,082
and simply walking around saying to oneself,

600
00:32:18,082 --> 00:32:19,082
now I am rearing a child,

601
00:32:19,082 --> 00:32:20,082
therefore I mustn't do these things,

602
00:32:20,082 --> 00:32:21,082
and I mustn't do those things,

603
00:32:21,082 --> 00:32:22,082
I must do that.

604
00:32:22,082 --> 00:32:23,082
Exactly.

605
00:32:23,082 --> 00:32:25,082
An entirely different thing.

606
00:32:25,082 --> 00:32:29,082
But one has to break the habit

607
00:32:29,082 --> 00:32:31,082
of seeing negation as prohibition.

608
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:33,082
And also, you see,

609
00:32:33,082 --> 00:32:37,082
with responsibility goes love, care,

610
00:32:37,082 --> 00:32:41,082
attention.

611
00:32:41,082 --> 00:32:44,082
Yes, earlier I was going to ask you about care

612
00:32:44,082 --> 00:32:48,082
in relation to responsibility.

613
00:32:48,082 --> 00:32:51,082
Something that would flow immediately.

614
00:32:51,082 --> 00:32:52,082
Naturally, sir.

615
00:32:52,082 --> 00:32:53,082
Naturally, yes.

616
00:32:53,082 --> 00:32:55,082
Not something that I would have to project

617
00:32:55,082 --> 00:32:57,082
that I needed to care for later.

618
00:32:57,082 --> 00:32:58,082
So I won't forget.

619
00:32:58,082 --> 00:33:00,082
But I would be with it.

620
00:33:00,082 --> 00:33:01,082
Yes.

621
00:33:01,082 --> 00:33:03,082
That involves a great deal too,

622
00:33:03,082 --> 00:33:06,082
because the mother,

623
00:33:06,082 --> 00:33:10,082
the mother depends on the child,

624
00:33:10,082 --> 00:33:12,082
and the child depends on the mother,

625
00:33:12,082 --> 00:33:14,082
or the father, whatever it is.

626
00:33:14,082 --> 00:33:19,082
So that dependence is cultivated,

627
00:33:19,082 --> 00:33:23,082
not only between the father and the mother,

628
00:33:23,082 --> 00:33:27,082
but depend on a teacher,

629
00:33:27,082 --> 00:33:33,082
depend on somebody to tell you what to do,

630
00:33:33,082 --> 00:33:36,082
depend on your guru.

631
00:33:36,082 --> 00:33:40,082
Yes, yes, I am following.

632
00:33:40,082 --> 00:33:43,082
So, gradually, the child, the man,

633
00:33:43,082 --> 00:33:48,082
is incapable of standing alone.

634
00:33:50,082 --> 00:33:51,082
And therefore you say,

635
00:33:51,082 --> 00:33:53,082
I must depend on my wife

636
00:33:53,082 --> 00:33:55,082
for my comfort, for my sex,

637
00:33:55,082 --> 00:33:57,082
for my this or that and the other thing.

638
00:33:57,082 --> 00:34:00,082
I am lost without her.

639
00:34:00,082 --> 00:34:03,082
And I am lost without my guru,

640
00:34:03,082 --> 00:34:05,082
without my teacher.

641
00:34:05,082 --> 00:34:06,082
It becomes difficult.

642
00:34:06,082 --> 00:34:10,081
It becomes so ridiculous.

643
00:34:10,081 --> 00:34:18,081
So, when the feeling of responsibility exists,

644
00:34:18,081 --> 00:34:22,081
all this disappears.

645
00:34:22,081 --> 00:34:26,081
You are responsible

646
00:34:26,081 --> 00:34:28,081
for your behaviour,

647
00:34:28,081 --> 00:34:30,081
for the way you bring up your children,

648
00:34:30,081 --> 00:34:33,081
for the way you treat a dog, a neighbour,

649
00:34:33,081 --> 00:34:34,081
the nature,

650
00:34:34,081 --> 00:34:36,081
everything is in your hands.

651
00:34:36,081 --> 00:34:42,081
Therefore, you have to become astonishingly careful

652
00:34:42,081 --> 00:34:43,081
what you do.

653
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:44,081
Careful, not,

654
00:34:44,081 --> 00:34:46,081
I must not do this and I must do that.

655
00:34:46,081 --> 00:34:47,081
Care.

656
00:34:47,081 --> 00:34:49,081
That means affection,

657
00:34:49,081 --> 00:34:52,081
that means consideration, diligence.

658
00:34:56,081 --> 00:35:01,082
All that goes with responsibility,

659
00:35:01,082 --> 00:35:05,082
which present society totally denies.

660
00:35:05,082 --> 00:35:12,082
When we begin to discuss

661
00:35:12,082 --> 00:35:16,082
the various gurus that are imported in this country,

662
00:35:16,082 --> 00:35:18,082
that's what they are doing,

663
00:35:18,082 --> 00:35:21,082
creating such mischief,

664
00:35:21,082 --> 00:35:24,082
making those people unfortunate,

665
00:35:24,082 --> 00:35:26,082
thoughtless people

666
00:35:26,082 --> 00:35:29,082
who want excitement join them,

667
00:35:29,082 --> 00:35:34,082
do all kinds of ridiculous, nonsensical things.

668
00:35:34,082 --> 00:35:40,082
So, we come back.

669
00:35:40,082 --> 00:35:45,082
Freedom implies responsibility.

670
00:35:45,082 --> 00:35:49,082
And therefore freedom, responsibility

671
00:35:49,082 --> 00:35:52,082
means care, diligence,

672
00:35:52,082 --> 00:35:54,082
not negligence,

673
00:35:54,082 --> 00:35:57,082
not doing what you want to do,

674
00:35:57,082 --> 00:36:00,082
which is what is happening in America.

675
00:36:00,082 --> 00:36:03,082
Do what you want to do.

676
00:36:04,082 --> 00:36:07,082
This permissiveness is just doing what you want to do,

677
00:36:07,082 --> 00:36:11,082
which is not freedom,

678
00:36:11,082 --> 00:36:16,082
which breeds irresponsibility.

679
00:36:19,082 --> 00:36:24,082
I met the other day in Delhi,

680
00:36:24,082 --> 00:36:28,082
New Delhi, a girl,

681
00:36:28,082 --> 00:36:33,082
and she has become reactivating.

682
00:36:33,082 --> 00:36:34,082
You follow, sir?

683
00:36:34,082 --> 00:36:36,082
Born in America, being a Christian,

684
00:36:36,082 --> 00:36:37,082
brought up all that,

685
00:36:37,082 --> 00:36:39,082
throws all that aside,

686
00:36:39,082 --> 00:36:41,082
becomes a Tibetan,

687
00:36:41,082 --> 00:36:43,082
which is the same thing in different words.

688
00:36:43,082 --> 00:36:46,082
Yes, as a Tibetan coming over here and doing it.

689
00:36:46,082 --> 00:36:48,082
It's all ridiculous.

690
00:36:48,082 --> 00:36:51,082
And I've known her some years,

691
00:36:51,082 --> 00:36:53,082
I said, where is your child?

692
00:36:53,082 --> 00:36:54,082
Who is sick?

693
00:36:54,082 --> 00:36:56,082
Oh, she says, I've left him

694
00:36:56,082 --> 00:37:01,082
with other liberated Tibetans.

695
00:37:01,082 --> 00:37:03,082
And I said,

696
00:37:03,082 --> 00:37:05,082
at six, you are the mother?

697
00:37:05,082 --> 00:37:06,082
She said, yes, sir,

698
00:37:06,082 --> 00:37:09,082
he is in very good hands.

699
00:37:09,082 --> 00:37:12,082
I come back next year and I ask,

700
00:37:12,082 --> 00:37:13,082
where is your child?

701
00:37:13,082 --> 00:37:15,082
Oh, he has become a Tibetan monk,

702
00:37:15,082 --> 00:37:16,082
who is seven.

703
00:37:16,082 --> 00:37:18,082
He is seven years old

704
00:37:18,082 --> 00:37:21,082
and has become a Tibetan monk.

705
00:37:21,082 --> 00:37:22,082
You understand, sir?

706
00:37:22,082 --> 00:37:25,082
Oh, yes, I do.

707
00:37:25,082 --> 00:37:29,082
The irresponsibility of it.

708
00:37:29,082 --> 00:37:30,082
Because the mother feels

709
00:37:30,082 --> 00:37:33,082
they know better than I do.

710
00:37:33,082 --> 00:37:36,082
I have become, I am a Tibetan

711
00:37:36,082 --> 00:37:40,082
and the lamas will help me to become that.

712
00:37:40,082 --> 00:37:42,082
It puts a rather sinister cast

713
00:37:42,082 --> 00:37:44,082
on that biblical statement,

714
00:37:44,082 --> 00:37:47,082
train up a child in the way he should go,

715
00:37:47,082 --> 00:37:48,582
and when he is old

716
00:37:48,582 --> 00:37:50,082
he will not depart from it.

717
00:37:50,082 --> 00:37:52,082
There is a sinister note in that, isn't there?

718
00:37:52,082 --> 00:37:54,082
Absolutely.

719
00:37:54,082 --> 00:37:56,082
So this is going on

720
00:37:56,082 --> 00:37:58,082
in the world all the time.

721
00:37:58,082 --> 00:38:02,082
And a man who is really serious,

722
00:38:02,082 --> 00:38:06,082
negates that.

723
00:38:06,082 --> 00:38:09,082
Because he understands the implications,

724
00:38:09,082 --> 00:38:13,082
the inwardness of all that.

725
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:16,082
So he has to deny it.

726
00:38:16,082 --> 00:38:19,082
It isn't a question of will or choice,

727
00:38:19,082 --> 00:38:26,082
he says that is too silly, too absurd.

728
00:38:26,082 --> 00:38:31,082
So freedom means responsibility

729
00:38:31,082 --> 00:38:32,082
and indifference.

730
00:38:32,082 --> 00:38:36,578
Infinite care.

731
00:38:36,578 --> 00:38:37,458
نعم

732
00:38:37,474 --> 00:38:43,674
The phrase that you just spoke, infinite care,

733
00:38:43,674 --> 00:38:47,684
would be totally impossible to what

734
00:38:47,684 --> 00:38:51,694
we mean by a finite being,

735
00:38:51,694 --> 00:38:57,454
unless the finite being did not betray the present.

736
00:38:57,454 --> 00:38:59,974
With not betraying the present, it's a negative again,

737
00:38:59,974 --> 00:39:01,514
it's a negation again.

738
00:39:01,514 --> 00:39:05,134
With not betraying the present,

739
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:06,934
which is not to say what

740
00:39:06,934 --> 00:39:08,734
will happen if it's not done.

741
00:39:08,734 --> 00:39:12,734
Sir, the word present, the now, is rather difficult.

742
00:39:12,734 --> 00:39:14,074
Oh yes.

743
00:39:14,074 --> 00:39:16,774
Philosophers love to call it the specious present.

744
00:39:16,774 --> 00:39:18,194
I don't know what philosophers say,

745
00:39:18,194 --> 00:39:21,974
I don't want to enter into all that speculative thinking.

746
00:39:21,974 --> 00:39:26,634
But the fact, what is the now?

747
00:39:26,634 --> 00:39:34,194
What is the act of now, the present?

748
00:39:34,194 --> 00:39:35,114
To understand the present,

749
00:39:35,114 --> 00:39:38,214
I must understand the past.

750
00:39:38,214 --> 00:39:40,354
Not history, I don't mean that.

751
00:39:40,354 --> 00:39:43,794
Understand myself as the past. I am the past.

752
00:39:43,794 --> 00:39:46,674
In terms of what we said earlier about knowledge.

753
00:39:46,674 --> 00:39:49,934
Yes, I am that.

754
00:39:49,934 --> 00:39:53,274
Therefore I must understand the

755
00:39:53,274 --> 00:39:56,614
present, the past, which is me.

756
00:39:56,614 --> 00:40:00,054
The me is the known.

757
00:40:00,054 --> 00:40:02,474
The me is not the unknown.

758
00:40:02,474 --> 00:40:04,354
I can imagine it's the unknown,

759
00:40:04,354 --> 00:40:05,114
but the me is the known.

760
00:40:05,114 --> 00:40:08,494
Actually, the fact is, the what is, is the known.

761
00:40:08,494 --> 00:40:12,294
That's me. I must understand myself.

762
00:40:12,294 --> 00:40:14,554
If I don't, the now is merely

763
00:40:14,554 --> 00:40:20,874
a continuation in modified form of the past.

764
00:40:20,874 --> 00:40:27,874
Therefore it's not the now, not the present.

765
00:40:27,874 --> 00:40:33,174
Therefore the me is the tradition, the knowledge,

766
00:40:33,174 --> 00:40:34,354
the in...

767
00:40:34,354 --> 00:40:38,813
all the complicated manoeuvres, cunning, you follow?

768
00:40:38,813 --> 00:40:39,313
All that.

769
00:40:39,313 --> 00:40:42,423
The despairs, the anxieties, the

770
00:40:42,423 --> 00:40:45,534
desire for success, fear, pleasure,

771
00:40:45,534 --> 00:40:49,314
all that is me.

772
00:40:49,314 --> 00:40:52,304
Since we are still involved

773
00:40:52,304 --> 00:40:55,294
in our discussion about relationship here,

774
00:40:55,294 --> 00:40:58,314
might we return a moment to where we were

775
00:40:58,314 --> 00:41:03,754
with respect to education and relationship?

776
00:41:03,754 --> 00:41:04,254
I...

777
00:41:04,254 --> 00:41:07,134
I want to be sure

778
00:41:07,134 --> 00:41:10,014
that I have understood you here.

779
00:41:10,014 --> 00:41:12,344
Let us say that one was

780
00:41:12,344 --> 00:41:14,674
fortunate enough to have a school

781
00:41:14,674 --> 00:41:19,294
where what you are pointing to was going on.

782
00:41:19,294 --> 00:41:20,694
We are going to, we are doing it.

783
00:41:20,694 --> 00:41:22,014
We have got several schools.

784
00:41:22,014 --> 00:41:23,534
Marvellous.

785
00:41:23,534 --> 00:41:25,054
Well, we'll have a chance

786
00:41:25,054 --> 00:41:26,574
to talk about that, won't we?

787
00:41:26,574 --> 00:41:27,014
Yes.

788
00:41:27,014 --> 00:41:33,014
Good, good.

789
00:41:33,014 --> 00:41:33,814
If I'm...

790
00:41:33,814 --> 00:41:38,904
If I'm current here, it would seem

791
00:41:38,904 --> 00:41:43,994
that if the teacher is totally present

792
00:41:43,994 --> 00:41:55,134
to the child, the child will feel this.

793
00:41:55,134 --> 00:41:57,594
The child won't have to be

794
00:41:57,594 --> 00:42:00,054
instructed in what this means then.

795
00:42:00,054 --> 00:42:01,374
Sir, that means...

796
00:42:01,374 --> 00:42:02,374
Is that right?

797
00:42:02,374 --> 00:42:02,874
Yes.

798
00:42:02,874 --> 00:42:03,674
But one has to...

799
00:42:03,674 --> 00:42:05,833
One has to find out what is

800
00:42:05,833 --> 00:42:07,993
the relationship of the teacher to the student.

801
00:42:07,993 --> 00:42:11,433
Yes. Yes, I quite see that. Of course.

802
00:42:11,433 --> 00:42:12,433
What is the relationship?

803
00:42:12,433 --> 00:42:17,433
Is he merely an informer,

804
00:42:17,433 --> 00:42:21,333
giving information to the child?

805
00:42:21,333 --> 00:42:22,594
Any machine can do that.

806
00:42:22,594 --> 00:42:24,053
Oh yes, the library is filled with...

807
00:42:24,053 --> 00:42:25,114
Any machine can.

808
00:42:25,114 --> 00:42:28,194
Or what is his relationship?

809
00:42:28,194 --> 00:42:32,674
Does he put himself on a pedestal up there,

810
00:42:32,674 --> 00:42:33,674
and the student down there?

811
00:42:33,674 --> 00:42:35,674
Yes.

812
00:42:35,674 --> 00:42:41,794
Or is the relationship between the teacher and the student,

813
00:42:41,794 --> 00:42:50,114
is it a relationship in which there is learning

814
00:42:50,114 --> 00:42:51,914
on the part of the

815
00:42:51,914 --> 00:42:53,714
teacher as well as the student?

816
00:42:53,714 --> 00:42:54,794
Learning.

817
00:42:54,794 --> 00:42:55,914
Yes.

818
00:42:55,914 --> 00:43:01,914
Not, I have learnt and I'm going to teach you.

819
00:43:01,914 --> 00:43:03,013
Therefore in that,

820
00:43:03,014 --> 00:43:07,134
there is a division between the teacher and the student.

821
00:43:07,134 --> 00:43:09,494
But when there is learning

822
00:43:09,494 --> 00:43:11,854
on the part of the teacher

823
00:43:11,854 --> 00:43:13,614
as well as on the part of the student,

824
00:43:13,614 --> 00:43:18,014
there is no division, both are learning.

825
00:43:18,014 --> 00:43:18,934
Yes.

826
00:43:18,934 --> 00:43:22,694
And therefore that relationship

827
00:43:22,694 --> 00:43:26,454
brings about a companionship.

828
00:43:26,454 --> 00:43:27,134
A sharing.

829
00:43:27,134 --> 00:43:27,934
A sharing.

830
00:43:27,934 --> 00:43:29,054
A sharing, yes.

831
00:43:29,054 --> 00:43:33,014
And taking a journey together.

832
00:43:33,014 --> 00:43:43,014
And therefore an infinite care on both sides.

833
00:43:43,014 --> 00:43:45,014
Uh-huh.

834
00:43:45,014 --> 00:43:51,014
So it means, how is the teacher to teach mathematics,

835
00:43:51,014 --> 00:43:54,014
or whatever it is, to the student,

836
00:43:54,014 --> 00:43:58,694
and yet teach it in such a way

837
00:43:58,694 --> 00:44:01,774
that you awaken the intelligence in the child,

838
00:44:01,774 --> 00:44:03,014
not about the child,

839
00:44:03,014 --> 00:44:05,014
but mathematics?

840
00:44:05,014 --> 00:44:08,014
No, of course not. No. Yes.

841
00:44:08,014 --> 00:44:18,014
And how do you bring this act of teaching

842
00:44:18,014 --> 00:44:20,014
in which there is order?

843
00:44:20,014 --> 00:44:24,014
Because mathematics means order.

844
00:44:24,014 --> 00:44:30,014
The highest form of order is mathematics.

845
00:44:30,014 --> 00:44:32,014
Now, how will you convey

846
00:44:32,014 --> 00:44:36,014
to the student in teaching mathematics

847
00:44:36,014 --> 00:44:43,014
that there should be order in his life?

848
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:46,014
Not order according to a blueprint,

849
00:44:46,014 --> 00:44:51,014
that's not order.

850
00:44:51,014 --> 00:44:52,014
You follow?

851
00:44:52,014 --> 00:44:53,014
Yes, yes.

852
00:44:53,014 --> 00:44:58,014
Therefore it's a creative teaching.

853
00:44:58,014 --> 00:45:01,014
Not creative, it's a teaching,

854
00:45:01,014 --> 00:45:05,014
an act of learning all the time.

855
00:45:05,014 --> 00:45:08,014
So it's a living thing.

856
00:45:08,014 --> 00:45:11,014
Uh-huh.

857
00:45:11,014 --> 00:45:13,014
That's something I've learnt,

858
00:45:13,014 --> 00:45:16,014
and I'm going to impart it to you.

859
00:45:16,014 --> 00:45:18,014
This reminds me of a little essay

860
00:45:18,014 --> 00:45:21,014
I read many years ago by Simone Weil,

861
00:45:21,014 --> 00:45:22,014
which she called,

862
00:45:22,014 --> 00:45:24,014
On Academic Studies.

863
00:45:24,014 --> 00:45:26,014
There's some title like that.

864
00:45:26,014 --> 00:45:30,014
And she said that every...

865
00:45:30,014 --> 00:45:33,014
one who teaches a subject

866
00:45:33,014 --> 00:45:41,014
is responsible for teaching the student

867
00:45:41,014 --> 00:45:44,014
the relation between what they're studying

868
00:45:44,014 --> 00:45:48,014
and the student's making a pure act of attention.

869
00:45:48,014 --> 00:45:49,014
I know, of course.

870
00:45:49,014 --> 00:45:51,014
And if this doesn't take place,

871
00:45:51,014 --> 00:45:53,014
the whole thing doesn't mean a thing.

872
00:45:53,014 --> 00:45:55,014
Sir, that just...

873
00:45:55,014 --> 00:45:57,014
One stops to think,

874
00:45:57,014 --> 00:45:58,014
what would a teacher say

875
00:45:58,014 --> 00:46:00,014
if a student walked up and looked at them

876
00:46:00,014 --> 00:46:02,014
and said, fine,

877
00:46:02,014 --> 00:46:05,014
we're studying calculus right now.

878
00:46:05,014 --> 00:46:09,014
Now, you tell me how I am to see this

879
00:46:09,014 --> 00:46:10,014
that I am pursuing

880
00:46:10,014 --> 00:46:12,014
in relation to my making

881
00:46:12,014 --> 00:46:14,014
a pure act of attention.

882
00:46:14,014 --> 00:46:18,014
Well, that would be likely a little embarrassing,

883
00:46:18,014 --> 00:46:20,014
except for the most unusual person

884
00:46:20,014 --> 00:46:22,014
who had this...

885
00:46:22,014 --> 00:46:24,014
who had a grasp of the present.

886
00:46:24,014 --> 00:46:25,014
Yes.

887
00:46:25,014 --> 00:46:27,014
So, sir, that's just it.

888
00:46:27,014 --> 00:46:30,014
What is the relationship of the teacher

889
00:46:30,014 --> 00:46:34,014
to the student in education?

890
00:46:34,014 --> 00:46:40,014
Is he training him merely to conform?

891
00:46:40,014 --> 00:46:45,014
Is he training him to cultivate mere memory,

892
00:46:45,014 --> 00:46:47,014
like a machine?

893
00:46:47,014 --> 00:46:52,014
Is he training or is he helping him

894
00:46:52,014 --> 00:46:55,014
to learn about life,

895
00:46:55,014 --> 00:46:58,014
not just about sex,

896
00:46:58,014 --> 00:46:59,014
life,

897
00:46:59,014 --> 00:47:02,014
but about immensity of living,

898
00:47:02,014 --> 00:47:06,014
the complexity of it?

899
00:47:06,014 --> 00:47:09,014
Which we are not doing.

900
00:47:09,014 --> 00:47:10,013
No.

901
00:47:10,013 --> 00:47:12,013
No, even in our language

902
00:47:12,013 --> 00:47:16,013
we refer students to subject matters.

903
00:47:16,013 --> 00:47:17,013
Yes, yes, yes.

904
00:47:17,013 --> 00:47:18,013
They take this, they take that,

905
00:47:18,013 --> 00:47:20,013
they take the other,

906
00:47:20,013 --> 00:47:23,014
and in fact there are prerequisites

907
00:47:23,014 --> 00:47:26,014
for taking these other things.

908
00:47:26,014 --> 00:47:28,014
And this builds a notion of education

909
00:47:28,014 --> 00:47:31,014
which has absolutely no relationship

910
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,014
to what...

911
00:47:32,014 --> 00:47:33,014
None at all.

912
00:47:33,014 --> 00:47:36,014
And yet, amazingly,

913
00:47:36,014 --> 00:47:39,014
in the catalogues of colleges and universities

914
00:47:39,014 --> 00:47:41,014
across the country,

915
00:47:41,014 --> 00:47:47,014
there is, in the first page or so,

916
00:47:47,014 --> 00:47:49,014
a rather pious remark

917
00:47:49,014 --> 00:47:52,014
about the relation between their going to school

918
00:47:52,014 --> 00:47:55,014
and the values of civilisation.

919
00:47:55,014 --> 00:47:57,014
And we have this whole...

920
00:47:57,014 --> 00:47:59,014
And that turns out to be

921
00:47:59,014 --> 00:48:01,014
learning a series of ideas.

922
00:48:01,014 --> 00:48:03,014
I don't know whether they do it any more,

923
00:48:03,014 --> 00:48:04,014
but they used to put the word

924
00:48:04,014 --> 00:48:05,014
character in there.

925
00:48:05,014 --> 00:48:07,014
They probably decided that's unpopular,

926
00:48:07,014 --> 00:48:09,014
might very well have dropped that out by now,

927
00:48:09,014 --> 00:48:10,014
I'm not sure.

928
00:48:10,014 --> 00:48:11,014
Yes, yes, yes,

929
00:48:11,014 --> 00:48:13,014
I'm following what you say.

930
00:48:13,014 --> 00:48:15,014
So, sir,

931
00:48:15,014 --> 00:48:21,014
when you feel responsible,

932
00:48:21,014 --> 00:48:25,014
there is a flowering of real affection.

933
00:48:25,014 --> 00:48:26,014
You understand, sir?

934
00:48:26,014 --> 00:48:27,014
Mm-hm.

935
00:48:27,014 --> 00:48:35,014
A flowering of care for a child.

936
00:48:35,014 --> 00:48:38,014
And you don't train him

937
00:48:38,014 --> 00:48:40,014
or cultivate or condition him

938
00:48:40,014 --> 00:48:42,014
to go and kill another

939
00:48:42,014 --> 00:48:45,014
for the sake of your country.

940
00:48:45,014 --> 00:48:46,014
You follow?

941
00:48:46,014 --> 00:48:49,014
All that is involved in it.

942
00:48:49,014 --> 00:48:51,014
Mm-hm.

943
00:48:55,014 --> 00:48:56,014
So,

944
00:48:56,014 --> 00:48:59,014
we come to a point

945
00:48:59,014 --> 00:49:01,014
where a human being,

946
00:49:01,014 --> 00:49:03,014
as he is now,

947
00:49:03,014 --> 00:49:09,014
so conditioned to be irresponsible,

948
00:49:09,014 --> 00:49:11,014
how is that...

949
00:49:11,014 --> 00:49:12,014
how...

950
00:49:12,014 --> 00:49:15,014
what are the serious people

951
00:49:15,014 --> 00:49:20,014
going to do with the irresponsible people?

952
00:49:20,014 --> 00:49:21,014
You understand?

953
00:49:21,014 --> 00:49:23,014
Mm-hm.

954
00:49:23,014 --> 00:49:25,014
Education, politics, religion,

955
00:49:25,014 --> 00:49:32,014
everything is making human beings irresponsible.

956
00:49:32,014 --> 00:49:33,014
Mm-hm.

957
00:49:33,014 --> 00:49:36,014
I'm not exaggerating, this is so.

958
00:49:36,014 --> 00:49:39,014
Oh, no, you're not exaggerating, yes.

959
00:49:39,014 --> 00:49:42,014
Now, I see this as a human being,

960
00:49:42,014 --> 00:49:45,014
I say, what am I to do?

961
00:49:45,014 --> 00:49:47,014
You follow, sir?

962
00:49:47,014 --> 00:49:48,014
Mm-hm.

963
00:49:48,014 --> 00:49:50,014
What is my responsibility

964
00:49:50,014 --> 00:49:54,014
in face of the irresponsible?

965
00:49:54,014 --> 00:49:56,014
Well, if it's to start anywhere,

966
00:49:56,014 --> 00:49:57,014
as we say in English,

967
00:49:57,014 --> 00:49:58,014
it must start at home.

968
00:49:58,014 --> 00:49:59,014
It would have to start with me.

969
00:49:59,014 --> 00:50:01,014
So I say, that's the whole point,

970
00:50:01,014 --> 00:50:03,014
I have to start with me.

971
00:50:03,014 --> 00:50:04,014
Right.

972
00:50:04,014 --> 00:50:08,014
Then if from that question arises,

973
00:50:08,014 --> 00:50:13,014
then you can't do anything about the irresponsible.

974
00:50:13,014 --> 00:50:14,014
No, exactly.

975
00:50:14,014 --> 00:50:15,014
No, sir.

976
00:50:15,014 --> 00:50:18,014
Something strange takes place.

977
00:50:18,014 --> 00:50:20,014
Oh, I misunderstood you, I'm sorry.

978
00:50:20,014 --> 00:50:22,014
What I meant by replying there is

979
00:50:22,014 --> 00:50:24,014
that I don't attack,

980
00:50:24,014 --> 00:50:25,014
I attack the irresponsible.

981
00:50:25,014 --> 00:50:26,014
No, no.

982
00:50:26,014 --> 00:50:27,014
No, yes, go ahead. Yes.

983
00:50:27,014 --> 00:50:31,014
Something strange takes place, which is,

984
00:50:31,014 --> 00:50:38,014
consciousness,

985
00:50:38,014 --> 00:50:42,014
the irresponsible consciousness is one thing.

986
00:50:42,014 --> 00:50:43,014
Yes.

987
00:50:43,014 --> 00:50:47,014
And the consciousness of responsibility is another.

988
00:50:47,014 --> 00:50:54,014
Now, when the human being is totally responsible,

989
00:50:54,014 --> 00:50:59,014
that responsibility unconsciously enters

990
00:50:59,014 --> 00:51:02,014
into the irresponsible mind.

991
00:51:02,014 --> 00:51:04,014
I don't know, I'm not saying anything.

992
00:51:04,014 --> 00:51:08,014
Yes, no, no, no, go ahead.

993
00:51:08,014 --> 00:51:11,014
Sir, look, I'm irresponsible.

994
00:51:11,014 --> 00:51:13,014
Suppose I'm irresponsible.

995
00:51:13,014 --> 00:51:15,014
You are responsible.

996
00:51:15,014 --> 00:51:22,014
You can't do anything consciously with me.

997
00:51:22,014 --> 00:51:23,014
Because the more you...

998
00:51:23,014 --> 00:51:28,014
Because the more you actively operate on me,

999
00:51:28,014 --> 00:51:30,014
the more I resist.

1000
00:51:30,014 --> 00:51:32,014
That's right. That's right.

1001
00:51:32,014 --> 00:51:34,014
That's what I meant by no attacking.

1002
00:51:34,014 --> 00:51:37,014
No attacking. I react violently to you.

1003
00:51:37,014 --> 00:51:38,014
I build a wall against you.

1004
00:51:38,014 --> 00:51:41,014
I hurt you. I do all kinds of things.

1005
00:51:41,014 --> 00:51:47,014
But you see that you cannot do anything consciously,

1006
00:51:47,014 --> 00:51:49,014
actively, let's put it that way.

1007
00:51:49,014 --> 00:51:50,014
Designedly.

1008
00:51:50,014 --> 00:51:52,014
Designedly.

1009
00:51:52,014 --> 00:51:53,014
Planned.

1010
00:51:53,014 --> 00:51:56,014
That's what they are all trying to do.

1011
00:51:56,014 --> 00:52:07,014
But if you can talk to me, to my unconscious...

1012
00:52:07,014 --> 00:52:09,014
Because the unconscious is much more active.

1013
00:52:09,014 --> 00:52:10,014
Oh, yes.

1014
00:52:10,014 --> 00:52:13,014
Much more alert, sees the danger much quicker

1015
00:52:13,014 --> 00:52:15,014
than the conscious.

1016
00:52:15,014 --> 00:52:19,014
So it's much more sensitive.

1017
00:52:19,014 --> 00:52:22,014
So if you can talk to me, to the unconscious,

1018
00:52:22,014 --> 00:52:26,014
that operates.

1019
00:52:26,014 --> 00:52:35,014
So you don't actively, designedly attack the irresponsible.

1020
00:52:35,014 --> 00:52:37,014
They have done it.

1021
00:52:37,014 --> 00:52:39,014
And they have made a mess of it.

1022
00:52:39,014 --> 00:52:42,014
Oh, yes, it compounds, complicates the thing further.

1023
00:52:42,014 --> 00:52:46,014
Whereas if you talk to him, you talk to me,

1024
00:52:46,014 --> 00:52:51,014
but your whole inward intention is to show

1025
00:52:51,014 --> 00:52:55,014
how irresponsible I am, what his responsibility means.

1026
00:52:55,014 --> 00:52:56,014
You follow?

1027
00:52:56,014 --> 00:52:57,014
You care.

1028
00:52:57,014 --> 00:52:59,014
In other words, you care for me.

1029
00:52:59,014 --> 00:53:00,014
Yes, yes.

1030
00:53:00,014 --> 00:53:03,014
I was chuckling because the complete and total opposite

1031
00:53:03,014 --> 00:53:08,014
crossed my mind, and it just seemed so absolutely absurd.

1032
00:53:08,014 --> 00:53:09,014
Yes.

1033
00:53:09,014 --> 00:53:11,014
No, I do.

1034
00:53:11,014 --> 00:53:15,014
You care for me because I am irresponsible.

1035
00:53:15,014 --> 00:53:16,014
You follow?

1036
00:53:16,014 --> 00:53:17,014
Exactly.

1037
00:53:17,014 --> 00:53:19,014
Therefore you care for me.

1038
00:53:19,014 --> 00:53:20,014
And therefore you are watching not to hurt me.

1039
00:53:20,014 --> 00:53:24,014
You follow?

1040
00:53:24,014 --> 00:53:28,014
In that way you penetrate very, very deeply

1041
00:53:28,014 --> 00:53:32,014
into my unconscious.

1042
00:53:32,014 --> 00:53:36,014
And that operates unknowingly when I am...

1043
00:53:36,014 --> 00:53:38,014
Suddenly I say, by Jove, how you are...

1044
00:53:38,014 --> 00:53:39,014
You follow?

1045
00:53:39,014 --> 00:53:41,014
That operates.

1046
00:53:41,014 --> 00:53:44,014
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

1047
00:53:44,014 --> 00:53:49,014
I have seen this, sir,

1048
00:53:49,014 --> 00:53:54,014
in operation, because I have talked for 50 years,

1049
00:53:54,014 --> 00:53:59,014
unfortunately or fortunately, to large audiences,

1050
00:53:59,014 --> 00:54:03,014
tremendous resistance to anything new.

1051
00:54:03,014 --> 00:54:04,014
Yes.

1052
00:54:04,014 --> 00:54:08,014
If I say, don't read sacred books,

1053
00:54:08,014 --> 00:54:10,014
which I say all the time,

1054
00:54:10,014 --> 00:54:15,014
because you are just conforming, obeying.

1055
00:54:15,014 --> 00:54:16,014
You are not living, you

1056
00:54:16,014 --> 00:54:17,014
are living according to some book

1057
00:54:17,014 --> 00:54:19,014
that you have read.

1058
00:54:19,014 --> 00:54:22,014
Immediately there is resistance.

1059
00:54:22,014 --> 00:54:24,014
Who are you to tell us?

1060
00:54:24,014 --> 00:54:25,014
Not to do something.

1061
00:54:25,014 --> 00:54:27,014
Not to do this or to do that.

1062
00:54:27,014 --> 00:54:29,514
So I say, all right, see,

1063
00:54:29,514 --> 00:54:32,014
I go on pointing out, pointing out.

1064
00:54:32,014 --> 00:54:35,014
I am not trying to change them.

1065
00:54:35,014 --> 00:54:37,014
I am not doing propaganda,

1066
00:54:37,014 --> 00:54:41,014
because I don't believe in propaganda, it is a lie.

1067
00:54:41,014 --> 00:54:43,014
So I say, look, look what

1068
00:54:43,014 --> 00:54:45,014
you do when you are irresponsible.

1069
00:54:45,014 --> 00:54:48,014
You are destroying your children.

1070
00:54:48,014 --> 00:54:52,014
You send them to war,

1071
00:54:52,014 --> 00:54:54,514
to be killed and to be

1072
00:54:54,514 --> 00:54:57,014
maimed and to kill and to maim.

1073
00:54:57,014 --> 00:54:59,014
It is that act of love, it

1074
00:54:59,014 --> 00:55:01,014
is that affection, it is that care.

1075
00:55:01,014 --> 00:55:03,014
Why do you do it?

1076
00:55:03,014 --> 00:55:06,014
And I go into it.

1077
00:55:06,014 --> 00:55:09,014
They get bewildered, they don't know what to do.

1078
00:55:09,014 --> 00:55:10,014
You know, sir?

1079
00:55:10,014 --> 00:55:15,014
So it begins to slowly seep in.

1080
00:55:15,014 --> 00:55:18,014
Well, at first it is such a shock.

1081
00:55:18,014 --> 00:55:23,014
It sounds positively subversive to some.

1082
00:55:23,014 --> 00:55:26,014
Oh, absolutely, absolutely subversive.

1083
00:55:26,014 --> 00:55:29,014
Of course, of course.

1084
00:55:29,014 --> 00:55:32,014
Yes, but...

1085
00:55:32,014 --> 00:55:36,014
So we enter into now something, which is,

1086
00:55:36,014 --> 00:55:40,014
my relationship to another,

1087
00:55:40,014 --> 00:55:44,014
when there is total responsibility

1088
00:55:44,014 --> 00:55:48,014
in which freedom and care go together,

1089
00:55:48,014 --> 00:55:52,014
I do not...

1090
00:55:52,014 --> 00:56:00,014
the mind has no image in relationship at all.

1091
00:56:00,014 --> 00:56:05,014
Because the image is the division.

1092
00:56:05,014 --> 00:56:09,014
Where there is care, there is no image, imagination,

1093
00:56:09,014 --> 00:56:12,014
no image.

1094
00:56:12,014 --> 00:56:16,014
This would lead us into

1095
00:56:16,014 --> 00:56:21,014
what perhaps later we could pursue,

1096
00:56:21,014 --> 00:56:23,014
love.

1097
00:56:23,014 --> 00:56:25,014
Ah, that's a tremendous thing.

1098
00:56:25,014 --> 00:56:27,014
Yes, yes.

1099
00:56:27,014 --> 00:56:31,014
Could we lay a little...

1100
00:56:31,014 --> 00:56:33,014
a few words before that?

1101
00:56:33,014 --> 00:56:35,014
I don't know necessarily that

1102
00:56:35,014 --> 00:56:37,014
next time we would do that,

1103
00:56:37,014 --> 00:56:40,014
but it would come naturally.

1104
00:56:40,014 --> 00:56:43,014
I've been listening to what you've been saying

1105
00:56:43,014 --> 00:56:46,014
and it has occurred to me that

1106
00:56:46,014 --> 00:56:51,014
if one is responsible

1107
00:56:51,014 --> 00:56:55,014
and care is continuous with that,

1108
00:56:55,014 --> 00:56:58,014
one would not fear,

1109
00:56:58,014 --> 00:57:01,014
one could not fear.

1110
00:57:01,014 --> 00:57:02,014
Yes, sir.

1111
00:57:02,014 --> 00:57:04,014
Not would not, could not.

1112
00:57:04,014 --> 00:57:06,014
Could not fear.

1113
00:57:06,014 --> 00:57:09,014
You see, that means really

1114
00:57:09,014 --> 00:57:13,014
one must understand fear.

1115
00:57:13,014 --> 00:57:15,014
One must understand fear.

1116
00:57:15,014 --> 00:57:16,014
Yes.

1117
00:57:16,014 --> 00:57:20,014
And also the pursuit of pleasure.

1118
00:57:20,014 --> 00:57:22,014
Those two go together,

1119
00:57:22,014 --> 00:57:25,014
they are not two separate things.

1120
00:57:25,014 --> 00:57:27,014
What I have...

1121
00:57:27,014 --> 00:57:29,014
what I've learned here

1122
00:57:29,014 --> 00:57:32,014
